// DO NOT DEPLOY THIS FILE.
//
// Storage security rules are owned by Lawslane/ — this repo shares the same
// Firebase project (studio-3946808940-28553), so only one ruleset is ever
// actually deployed. Edit and deploy from Lawslane/storage.rules instead.
// See LAWSLANE-ECOSYSTEM.md and LAWSLANE-PLAN-01 (0.2) for context.
//
// This file is intentionally NOT valid rules syntax, so `firebase deploy`
// will fail loudly here instead of silently overwriting the real rules in
// production with a stale or weaker copy.
//
// NOTE: firestore.rules got this tripwire earlier but storage.rules did not,
// which left `firebase deploy --only storage` as an unguarded path that
// silently downgraded production storage rules (opening every contract file
// and company vault to any signed-in user, and dropping upload validation).
STOP: storage rules owned by Lawslane/. Do not deploy from this repo.
